    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d178">

                <pb facs="0336" n="224" xml:id="pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">693.11241 Manchuria/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-06-10T18:00:00-04:00">June 10, 1935—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>156. Your 244, June 6, 1 p.m. Department authorizes Legation to instruct
                    Ballantine as suggested in the penultimate paragraph of your telegram. The
                    Department will await with interest a report of Ballantine’s informal
                    discussion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
